\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The 2000--2004 reversal, cell by cell. Technology-class registrations filed 2000--2004 and settled at the five-year proof, split by their dominant $T=50$ theme and by whether their description names the internet; every theme$\times $internet cell with at least 5{,}000 registrations is shown. Each point is the failure contrast between the most leading and the most lagging fifth, quintiles cut within the cell, with a 95\% binomial interval. Points left of zero are cells where leading filings survived more often. Sizes, shares of the era's leading fifth and failure rates are in Supplementary Material \S  S2.}}{18}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
